{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"8f879536012842e8ddc896470e33cfa63fca6e6aa9baaef0d4065f2f38e176c7","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar CLI command parsing","key_entities":["rebar comment","rebar create","rebar edit","rebar session-log","rebar tag","rebar untag","rebar archive","rebar set-verify-commands","--body-file","--body","--","Usage:"],"problem_keywords":["CLI argument parsing","positional argument","flag-like token","silent data loss","exit code masking","comment storage","durability"],"propositions":["rebar comment <id> --body-file <path> stores the literal flag string instead of the intended body and exits 0, destroying the record","positional-body commands accept flag-looking tokens as body content without rejection, allowing silent data loss in the durable ticket store","flag-like arguments are stored and surplus positionals are truncated, resulting in double loss of intended content","the CLI must reject body arguments beginning with - and provide -- escape hatch for legitimate dash-prefixed values","the guard against flag-like positional bodies must be consistently applied across all positional-body commands in the CLI surface"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787295649587592001,"uuid":"84df77c9-57a2-40ab-893d-4b13939643ca"}